# Build context for services/dvswitch/docker/Dockerfile is `services/dvswitch`
# (docker-compose.yml: `context: ..`), NOT the repo root — so the repo-root
# .dockerignore does not apply here and this directory needs its own.
#
# Found 2026-08-14 while investigating a SonarQube CRITICAL (docker:S6470) on
# the Dockerfile's `COPY . /opt/ticketscad-dvswitch/services/dvswitch/`: the
# documented install (`cd services/dvswitch/docker && cp .env.example .env`,
# fill in DMR_MASTER_PASSWORD and DMR_BEARER_TOKEN, `docker compose up -d
# --build`) creates docker/.env INSIDE this build context, and with no
# .dockerignore here it was baked straight into the image layer — readable
# from the image itself (`docker save` / `docker history` / registry access)
# even though the same values are also passed at runtime via `environment:`.
# Following the docs exactly was what caused it.

docker/.env
docker/.env.*
!docker/.env.example

# Standard hygiene for a Python build context.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.git
.gitignore
